<title>USA: CIBER plans 1.25 mln share offering.</title>
<headline>CIBER plans 1.25 mln share offering.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>CIBER Inc said on Tuesday it planned to offer 1.25 million shares of common stock at a price of $30 per share.</p>
<p>CIBER said it was offering 423,077 shares and certain selling shareholders were offering 826,923 shares. CIBER said it had also granted the underwriters a 30-day option to purchase up to 187,500 additional shares to cover any over-allotments.</p>
<p>The comany said its investment bankers were Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, J.P. Morgan Securities Inc and Hanifen, Imhoff Inc.</p>
<p>CIBER provides information technology consulting.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
